{"custom_id": "b31ac58b219b8dac96859631f0aa615c0c1241e28ab7ae39", "meta": {"loop": "topk4L01", "task": "generate_moderation_principle_2", "occurrence": 0, "attempt": 0, "max_tokens": 128000, "prompt_sha256": "34b7e971b8f86cfd82279c03a551a41164d3a9294906fde868674348c1d4791d", "prompt_chars": 6007}, "batch_id": "msgbatch_01XqPah1Z52Aa79TvrnDBTJ8", "saved_utc": "2026-10-22T12:33:38+00:00", "message": {"id": "msg_011CgHHATwzvstY2QQa1XfU9", "container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "- **Reference-Frame Rule for Generic Condition Nouns:**\n  - **IF** a generic condition noun (a sign, symptom, or broad condition category, not a named disease, eponym, or acronym) is the head of a noun phrase introduced by a patient-presentation frame, such as a participial or prepositional phrase attributing the condition to an individual patient subject, **THEN** label it **SpecificDisease** (instance-level), even when it is coordinated with other conditions or modified by an adjective.\n  - **IF** the same kind of noun appears under a type-level predicate (a predicate describing a disease category's defining features or outcomes) or as a descriptive feature of a named disease entity, **THEN** label it **DiseaseClass**.\n  - **Negative constraint:** This rule does **NOT** apply to named diseases, eponyms, or acronyms, which remain SpecificDisease in every frame. It also does not apply when the subject is a disease type rather than an individual, or when no governing predicate can be identified. In those cases, do not decide the label from list structure or modifiers alone; fall back to the entity definitions and standard guideline conventions.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2298, "output_tokens": 1411, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 1031}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}